you don't really like Mimi.

499
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:51,101
- Mmm.
- I can tell just by looking.

500
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:54,354
This is cause I talk to her, right?

501
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:56,148
You can't stand me talking to her?

502
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:00,902
I wouldn't say I can't stand it.
I don't mind you talking to her.

503
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:03,363
But I don't want to see it
right in front of me.

504
00:22:05,073 --> 00:22:08,118
So now I'm starting
to lose track of my own feelings.

505
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:09,995
Mmm.

506
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:11,788
Well,

507
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:14,791
I get how you feel,
but it's also the environment we're in.

508
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:16,501
Which is why I said it's fine.

509
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,922
What you do is up to you.

510
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,800
<i>This isn't good.</i>

511
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,218
<i>This isn't good.</i>

512
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:27,971
This place is great!

513
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:28,972
BUDDHA LEAN

514
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,182
Are the seats assigned?

515
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:31,558
Just sit wherever you like.

516
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,185
The seats are different every day.

517
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,728
They change every day.

518
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:38,357
So Tai-chan really wants
to sit there after all!

519
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,275
- Then I'll sit on my knees.
- Why not here?

520
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:42,652
All right.

521
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:44,988
I'm having so much fun today.

522
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,656
- Already?
- I'm having so much fun.

523
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:47,699
It's so fun here.

524
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:50,035
I'm looking forward
to talking with the guys

525
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:51,745
just as much as I am with the girls.

526
00:22:51,828 --> 00:22:52,746
- Yeah?
- Is that so?

527
00:22:52,829 --> 00:22:54,831
That's why, if we do have a fight,

528
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:56,375
I want things to be good with us.

529
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:58,752
- You like to drink with the guys.
- I love drinking with the guys.

530
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:01,380
I had friends over all the time.
My place was a hangout spot.

531
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:02,672
I was always the host.

532
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:03,799
I see.

533
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:07,719
Even if we'd fought at first,
we could still be talking like this now.

534
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:09,262
It's not good to hold a grudge.

535
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:10,472
- True.
- Just settle it.

536
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:12,391
It would've been fine if we clashed.

537
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:15,644
Because I was confident
that we'd become friends afterward.

538
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:18,313
<i>All the guys are good guys.</i>

539
00:23:19,314 --> 00:23:23,151
I don't know. It's like,
let's say Ryopi and I started dating.

540
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,237
I don't need to meet his female friends.

541
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,363
You mentioned that.

542
00:23:26,446 --> 00:23:29,241
I don't want to see him
being friendly with other girls.

543
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,535
That's when Mimi came in and…

544
00:23:32,327 --> 00:23:33,453
you two were talking.

545
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:34,871
- I mean, you're friends.
- Mmm-hmm.

546
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:37,332
I understand that,
but I don't want to see it in front of me.

547
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:40,419
For Ryopi, I know he can't ignore you.

548
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:42,337
I mean, I understand that.

549
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:44,881
- I know it's not your fault, Mimi.
- I get that.

550
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,425
I get it, but still,

551
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:49,469
I'm just saying, in life,
you're going to meet people

552
00:23:49,553 --> 00:23:51,513
who run businesses and people who work.

553
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:54,474
I know that,
but I don't want to see it in front of me.

554
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,685
So, I'm rooting for him
when it comes to work.

555
00:23:56,768 --> 00:23:58,687
On the other hand, I'm also a hostess,

556
00:23:58,770 --> 00:24:01,648
so I also have opportunities
to talk to men,

557
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:02,941
I understand that.

558
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:07,154
But even though you say you understand,
I don't think you really do.

559
00:24:07,237 --> 00:24:09,406
Really? I do understand, though.

560
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:16,288
I see work as work,
and love as love, okay?

561
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:18,623
- No, you don't.
- Huh? I do. I'm being serious.

562
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,208
I'm not lying.

563
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:22,335
No, you're 20 now, right?

564
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:25,964
The world you see at 20 is only this big.

565
00:24:26,047 --> 00:24:27,340
<i>Wow, that's amazing!</i>

566
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:28,967
You just don't understand it.

567
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:32,220
I can tell you want to understand
but you can't. Honestly.

568
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:34,431
I'm sorry,
but I don't think you understand.

569
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:36,224
You're 20. We're 29.

570
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:43,398
- Wow, crazy.
- This has gotten pretty intense.

571
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:44,524
What's going on here?

572
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:47,027
If I came home and saw
that look in her eyes,

573
00:24:47,110 --> 00:24:49,404
- I'd close the door.
- You would close it, right?

574
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:54,159
It's true that Rinrin has been
acting difficult for a while.

575
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:57,412
And it seems like she's starting
to lose track of her feelings.

576
00:24:57,496 --> 00:25:01,082
Yeah, so this feels like
Mimi had no choice but to speak up.

577
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:02,501
Yeah, it was too much.

578
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:04,878
- That's right.
- She kept going on and on about it.

579
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,463
- Someone had to say it.
- Someone had to.

580
00:25:06,546 --> 00:25:08,131
I guess you're right.

581
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:10,217
Maybe she simply can't separate

582
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:12,802
this current situation
from her past trauma.

583
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:16,723
Maybe she's getting flashbacks
of various things, probably.

584
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:18,099
- I see.
- The closer they get.

585
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:20,352
But that's a separate issue
from this relationship.

586
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:21,645
- Well, that's true.
- Right?

587
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:23,772
- This was something, huh?
- Really.

588
00:25:23,855 --> 00:25:24,940
The world you see at 20.

589
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:26,566
This is just Buddha.

590
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:28,151
Buddha? Reclining Buddha?

591
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:31,238
- It's Buddha vibes.
- It's this, right? This is indeed Buddha.

592
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,073
- It's Buddha.
- I see it.

593
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:35,033
She's even dressed
kind of like Buddha, right?

594
00:25:35,116 --> 00:25:37,202
In fact, her expression is similar too.

595
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:39,287
Ayacheru is the most drama-free.

596
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:40,580
She really is.

597
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:41,957
That little voice.

598
00:25:45,502 --> 00:25:48,046
- That's not what she sounds like.
- She doesn't sound like that.

599
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,631
Doesn't she? Like a calf somehow…

600
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:51,633
- She's not a calf.
- She's the only one.

601
00:25:51,716 --> 00:25:54,511
- You're exactly right.
- She's truly like water in a desert.

602
00:25:54,594 --> 00:25:56,513
Truly like an oasis. Honest water.

603
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:57,889
Honest water.

604
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:08,858
- <i>Okay.</i>
- <i>More basketball you hate.</i>

605
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,151
<i>Yeah, there it is.</i>

606
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,237
<i>- Like in prison.</i>
<i>- Like local delinquents.</i>

607
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:13,530
<i>Right, exactly.</i>

608
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,492
Nice!

609
00:26:18,743 --> 00:26:20,829
<i>Kamaken is really good.</i>

610
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:23,540
LIVING ROOM

611
00:26:23,623 --> 00:26:25,250
- Yo.
- What the heck's this?

612
00:26:25,333 --> 00:26:26,459
Morning.

613
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:27,669
When'd you go to bed?

614
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:32,257
You know how you said
you were drunk last night?

615
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:35,635
Is that the only reason
you said that stuff to me?

616
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,138
That's a secret.

617
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:39,222
What do you mean?

618
00:26:45,729 --> 00:26:48,064
<i>The weather is nice today,</i>

619
00:26:48,148 --> 00:26:50,233
<i>so we will have a barbecue at the beach.</i>

620
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:56,364
<i>Since it is a barbecue,</i>
<i>alcohol will be allowed.</i>

621
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:58,617
<i>Everyone, please get ready.</i>

622
00:26:58,700 --> 00:26:59,826
Let's go!

623
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:02,245
- Let's go.
- Let's get to it, everyone!

624
00:27:02,329 --> 00:27:04,039
Let's do this thing!

625
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:06,458
<i>Wow, this is such a gorgeous view.</i>

626
00:27:06,541 --> 00:27:08,501
<i>Okinawa is the best.</i>

627
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:11,504
<i>Badly in Love!</i>

628
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:13,381
The greatest show!

629
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:14,674
With the greatest cast!

630
00:27:14,758 --> 00:27:16,968
These 11 people

631
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:19,638
will drink best champagne…

632
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:21,431
and the best rosé! Here we go!

633
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:23,975
Three, two, one.

634
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:25,226
All right!

635
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:29,314
- Thank you! Here you go.
- Cheers!

636
00:27:29,397 --> 00:27:31,358
Cheers!

637
00:27:31,441 --> 00:27:32,734
Let's have fun!

638
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:34,861
<i>Wow, this must be so much fun.</i>

639
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:38,657
I'm gonna dump this on you.

640
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:45,914
So good!

641
00:27:53,046 --> 00:27:54,547
- Here, here.
- Thanks.

642
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:56,007
Now, both of you.

643
00:27:56,549 --> 00:27:58,134
Ready, set…

644
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:03,598
Go for it!

645
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:07,519
- What was that?
- Last longer than that.

646
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:09,062
Wow, incredible!

647
00:28:09,145 --> 00:28:11,481
- You're so strong.
- Did you see that?

648
00:28:11,564 --> 00:28:13,233
- He's strong!
- Very impressive.

649
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:14,401
The winner is Kamaken!

650
00:28:14,484 --> 00:28:15,985
Come on, let's go again!

651
00:28:16,069 --> 00:28:18,405
Knocked him over.
That shocked me just now!

652
00:28:18,488 --> 00:28:20,240
Come at me, Kazuma!

653
00:28:20,323 --> 00:28:23,535
All right, let's start this round fresh!

654
00:28:23,618 --> 00:28:25,161
Ready, set. Let's go!

655
00:28:25,245 --> 00:28:26,454
That's good.

656
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,997
Oh no, that spot's not great.

657
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:29,332
- Whoa!
- You can do it!

658
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:32,419
- Oh, no! Come on, come on!
- You're so strong.

659
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,630
- I couldn't do anything.
- Impressive.

660
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:36,548
Insane!

661
00:28:36,631 --> 00:28:39,843
Now it's time for Ryupi to play.
Come on. Get out there!

662
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:42,429
- Come on, Ryupi, it's your turn now.
- Who the heck is Ryupi?

663
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:44,597
No, I only fight people I can beat.

664
00:28:44,681 --> 00:28:46,725
And since Maru isn't here, I forfeit!

665
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:50,270
Wait, hold on. Just go once.

666
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:52,272
- Kamaken!
- Ryopi! Ryopi!

667
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:54,357
Hey, Sara, let's talk.

668
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:55,442
Sure.

669
00:28:56,359 --> 00:28:58,069
I'm super frustrated.

670
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,656
You picked the wrong fight.

671
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,825
You definitely picked the wrong fight.

672
00:29:03,908 --> 00:29:05,577
But I really thought I could win.

673
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:08,329
Well, it's not like you can beat everyone.

674
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,748
But, you know, I weigh more than him.

675
00:29:09,831 --> 00:29:11,291
Yeah, that's true.

676
00:29:11,374 --> 00:29:15,086
When someone's that heavy,
sweep their leg and it's over.

677
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:16,755
How do you know?

678
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:20,383
I've done MMA, judo, kickboxing as well.

679
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:23,011
- I didn't know that. You've done a lot.
- Yeah, I've also done Muay Thai.

680
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:25,555
- You're stronger than me!
- I probably wouldn't lose.

681
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:29,058
- Should we have a sumo match?
- I won't lose.

682
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:30,810
That would be fun for me.

683
00:29:32,896 --> 00:29:36,149
I've been wanting to talk about tattoos
with you for a while. Can we?

684
00:29:36,983 --> 00:29:39,402
<i>He's finally getting to see her tattoos.</i>

685
00:29:39,986 --> 00:29:42,489
These cherry blossoms
were originally pink, right?

686
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,491
The cherry blossoms on top were pink.

687
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,910
- Wow.
- And yeah, I had those redone.

688
00:29:47,535 --> 00:29:51,372
A Western tattoo artist did it,
so it ended up really colorful.

689
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:53,833
Oh, so this is one large
back tattoo, and the artist was--

690
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:55,210
- It was two.
- Oh, two artists.

691
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:57,253
Yeah, I had it done first in Okinawa.

692
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:59,964
Then, I asked someone
in Nara to work on me,

693
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:02,842
and I went over there to have them do it.

694
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:05,386
But you can't finish it in one go, right?
You had to go back?

695
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:08,056
Yeah, I took two overnight trips.
So, like, ten hours in two days.

696
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:09,641
- Seriously?
- That's right.

697
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:12,060
Wow, that's incredible.
Ten hours in two days?

698
00:30:12,143 --> 00:30:13,144
I was shaking.

699
00:30:13,228 --> 00:30:15,855
I was wondering
why I was paying to hurt so bad.

700
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:17,524
But you don't regret it?

701
00:30:17,607 --> 00:30:19,317
No, I don't regret it.

702
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:23,613
But, you know, I'll probably regret it
when I have kids in the future.

703
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:25,740
- Mmm.
- I'm sure.

704
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,992
- You didn't get the eye of the phoenix?
- No.

705
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:31,037
Well, if there's ever
a good time to do it,

706
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:32,539
I'll probably add that part then.

707
00:30:32,622 --> 00:30:35,875
It's about timing? Well, if I became
a tattoo artist by then, can I do it?

708
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:36,960
I'll consider it.

709
00:30:41,631 --> 00:30:43,132
This is nice, huh?

710
00:30:43,216 --> 00:30:45,677
- I haven't been on a swing in forever.
- Yeah, it's great here.

711
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:49,389
- It's hard to know you like someone.
- It's really hard.

712
00:30:49,472 --> 00:30:51,224
To tell you straight, I can't tell.

713
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:53,977
Can you tell me what she just said?

714
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:56,479
I only caught the
"To tell you straight" part.

715
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:58,273
"To tell you straight, I can't tell."

716
00:30:58,356 --> 00:30:59,566
You haven't figured it out?

717
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:01,901
- I haven't.
- What? You don't know, huh?

718
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:04,195
- That's not quite it.
- You're feeling unsure?

719
00:31:04,279 --> 00:31:05,655
What are you actually feeling, then?

720
00:31:06,406 --> 00:31:08,825
I'm curious to know
what you're actually feeling.

721
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,160
Oh, about who?

722
00:31:11,244 --> 00:31:12,120
About me.

723
00:31:14,664 --> 00:31:18,251
Wait, so for me, there was a part of me
that was always having doubt.

724
00:31:19,335 --> 00:31:20,169
About what?

725
00:31:20,253 --> 00:31:21,629
Well, so, um,

726
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:25,258
to tell you straight, I figured
you just found me easy to talk to.

727
00:31:25,341 --> 00:31:30,513
And I figured that you didn't have any
true romantic feelings for me or anything.

728
00:31:30,597 --> 00:31:34,893
I thought you probably just found me
easy to talk to, and that's all.

729
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:36,978
- You thought so?
- Yeah, that's right.

730
00:31:37,061 --> 00:31:39,731
- Well, it's been about a week now,
- Yeah.

731
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:44,068
and, well, the person I like the most
at this stage hasn't changed.

732
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:45,486
It's still you, Aya.

733
00:31:49,324 --> 00:31:52,285
Well, you know,
after talking to you today,

734
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:54,120
I do think it's you.

735
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:56,039
That you're the one I like the most.

736
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:57,457
Maybe… yeah.

737
00:31:59,542 --> 00:32:01,669
- Awkward!
- Okay, let's get that in writing.

738
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:03,087
It's embarrassing to say this stuff.

739
00:32:03,171 --> 00:32:04,756
<i>She's so adorable.</i>

740
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:05,840
It is, isn't it?

741
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:08,009
- Yes, it's embarrassing.
