<i>They're all scary, sort of.</i>

981
00:42:43,435 --> 00:42:45,479
- Here he comes!
- What do you think you're doing?

982
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:47,022
I'm scared, I'm scared!

983
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,649
Get over here, Kazuma!

984
00:42:48,732 --> 00:42:50,317
I've been waiting for you!

985
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,236
This is way too deep!

986
00:42:52,319 --> 00:42:54,113
- Hey, guys!
- You're crazy!

987
00:42:54,196 --> 00:42:55,698
It's freezing in here!

988
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:58,534
You were taking too long, damn it!

989
00:42:59,243 --> 00:43:01,245
Damn it! Why won't you go under?

990
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:02,997
- You guys are gonna drown!
- Okay, okay, okay!

991
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:05,040
He's gonna drown! No!

992
00:43:05,124 --> 00:43:06,959
Come on! He'll drown.

993
00:43:13,465 --> 00:43:15,217
Kazuma, let's talk over there.

994
00:43:15,301 --> 00:43:17,303
- The two of us? Sure.
- The two of us.

995
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,975
So, look man.

996
00:43:23,058 --> 00:43:25,060
There was a moment
you seriously ticked me off.

997
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:25,978
- Me?
- Mmm.

998
00:43:26,061 --> 00:43:27,104
What was it?

999
00:43:27,187 --> 00:43:31,191
Well, Kazuma, when you came swimming
toward us, I tried to high-five you.

1000
00:43:32,359 --> 00:43:33,694
I was like, "All right, you made it!"

1001
00:43:33,777 --> 00:43:35,195
But then…

1002
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,780
you threw your whole weight on me.

1003
00:43:36,864 --> 00:43:38,991
I pretty much almost drowned, straight-up.

1004
00:43:40,034 --> 00:43:42,745
Well, I seriously held back, to be honest.

1005
00:43:42,828 --> 00:43:44,455
You don't need to hold back at all.

1006
00:43:44,538 --> 00:43:46,248
It's not about me
not needing to hold back.

1007
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:49,752
It's like,
if I didn't need to hold back, you know,

1008
00:43:49,835 --> 00:43:51,795
I would've taken you down right there.

1009
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:54,006
You should've done it then.

1010
00:43:54,089 --> 00:43:56,258
- You should've just done it then.
- Sorry?

1011
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:58,093
If that's how you felt,
you should've done it.

1012
00:43:58,177 --> 00:44:00,471
If you don't back off,
I might lay you out.

1013
00:44:01,263 --> 00:44:03,182
Lay me out?
If you think you can do it, try me.

1014
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:05,601
- Wanna go, then?
- Yeah. No, come at me, seriously.

1015
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:06,977
Yeah. Yeah.

1016
00:44:08,687 --> 00:44:10,814
Why are you acting so calm, man?

1017
00:44:10,898 --> 00:44:12,066
What's your problem?

1018
00:44:12,149 --> 00:44:13,233
Come at me. Huh?

1019
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:15,361
What's your problem?

1020
00:44:19,698 --> 00:44:22,368
- Security, stop them!
- Security, where have you gone off to?

1021
00:44:22,451 --> 00:44:23,994
No… Don't throw hands, don't throw hands.

1022
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:26,205
- Come at me.
- Hey, Maru.

1023
00:44:26,288 --> 00:44:27,998
- Maru, be careful.
- Chill out.

1024
00:44:28,082 --> 00:44:30,250
<i>- </i>Kazuma.
- <i>Maru is here.</i>

1025
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:31,877
<i>Security, hurry up!</i>

1026
00:44:31,960 --> 00:44:33,879
<i>Maru is the last person who can stop this.</i>

1027
00:44:33,962 --> 00:44:35,589
<i>Maru can't possibly stop this!</i>

1028
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:37,800
<i>- Security, hurry up!</i>
<i>- Maru can't stop this!</i>

1029
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:39,593
What's wrong?

1030
00:44:40,636 --> 00:44:42,930
- You watch yourself.
- Right back at you.

1031
00:44:43,013 --> 00:44:44,223
Why is this happening?

1032
00:44:44,306 --> 00:44:46,433
- Oh, no, it's way late.
- Too late!

1033
00:44:46,517 --> 00:44:47,851
It's way late.

1034
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:49,436
I could eat you for breakfast.

1035
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:51,814
Oh, bring it on.
I can't wait for you to prove it.

1036
00:44:51,897 --> 00:44:53,107
I'll remember this.

1037
00:44:53,190 --> 00:44:54,983
- Hey, Kamaken.
- Do whatever you want.

1038
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:55,901
Hey.

1039
00:44:55,984 --> 00:44:57,236
You wanna fight, just say when.

1040
00:44:57,319 --> 00:44:58,987
- Bring it on.
- Come with me.

1041
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:05,160
I'm gonna kill that guy.

1042
00:45:06,870 --> 00:45:07,955
I don't care anymore.

1043
00:45:08,038 --> 00:45:09,456
I'll get expelled.

1044
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:10,791
I said, let go of me!

1045
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:12,710
Come at me, you bastard!

1046
00:45:12,793 --> 00:45:14,169
Hey, Kamaken.

1047
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:15,879
Hey, Kamaken. Look away for a second.

1048
00:45:15,963 --> 00:45:19,007
- Hey, hey.
- Let's sit over here for now.

1049
00:45:19,091 --> 00:45:21,009
- I'm seriously ticked off, really.
- I get it.

1050
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,595
I get it, but it's only your first day.

1051
00:45:24,263 --> 00:45:26,223
This is his first day? Are you kidding?

1052
00:45:26,306 --> 00:45:28,726
- I'm sorry, it is, isn't it?
- That's right.

1053
00:45:32,896 --> 00:45:33,731
Have a seat.

1054
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:35,733
What's going on? Is it the alcohol?

1055
00:45:35,816 --> 00:45:37,151
Well, yeah.

1056
00:45:38,026 --> 00:45:39,319
Why were you irritated?

1057
00:45:40,863 --> 00:45:45,534
Me and Sara, we were chatting and started
talking about going into the ocean.

1058
00:45:47,494 --> 00:45:49,663
And then, well, Kazuma--

1059
00:45:49,747 --> 00:45:51,999
I mean, I knew he was interested in Sara.

1060
00:45:52,082 --> 00:45:53,125
He just…

1061
00:45:54,209 --> 00:45:56,420
This is the stage
where you want to chat, right?

1062
00:45:56,503 --> 00:45:58,172
- With who?
- With everyone.

1063
00:45:59,131 --> 00:46:00,924
Honestly, I don't care if I'm expelled.

1064
00:46:01,550 --> 00:46:03,093
There's no one I'm interested in.

1065
00:46:03,844 --> 00:46:05,053
Why are you being like this?

1066
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:08,682
- Mmm, it's like--
- I mean, is this what you came here to do?

1067
00:46:09,975 --> 00:46:12,269
- You haven't even gotten to know me yet.
- Well, that's true.

1068
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:14,062
You liked me at first impression, right?

1069
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,063
Mmm.

1070
00:46:15,147 --> 00:46:17,024
Now I feel like "what was that?"

1071
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:18,734
I mean, that's true but… But it's also--

1072
00:46:18,817 --> 00:46:21,487
That makes me wonder
what kind of man you are.

1073
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:22,446
What's up?

1074
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:25,115
We're just chatting.
You don't know what happened?

1075
00:46:29,369 --> 00:46:30,829
I started to get irritated,

1076
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:33,624
- Did it gradually start to bubble up?
- Yeah, exactly.

1077
00:46:35,876 --> 00:46:37,961
You wanted him to know,
"This isn't what you think it is."

1078
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:39,171
I wanna take him.

1079
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:41,965
Come on, you can't. No, no, no, seriously.

1080
00:46:42,049 --> 00:46:43,634
Hey, hey, hey, I'm begging you.

1081
00:46:43,717 --> 00:46:45,385
Hey, we're both transfer students.

1082
00:46:45,469 --> 00:46:46,970
- It's seriously lame.
- Kamaken.

1083
00:46:47,054 --> 00:46:48,972
He's clumsy, for sure.

1084
00:46:49,056 --> 00:46:52,810
But I think he's coming to talk,
so don't lay a hand on him and just talk.

1085
00:46:55,854 --> 00:46:57,356
- Relax.
- I told you, I'm calm.

1086
00:46:58,690 --> 00:47:00,150
We're gonna try to talk.

1087
00:47:00,901 --> 00:47:03,529
Don't say "try to talk."
Say "we will talk."

1088
00:47:05,072 --> 00:47:06,365
We're back to Ethics, aren't we?

1089
00:47:06,448 --> 00:47:07,699
Yeah, we're back.

1090
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:09,368
Show me a reality dating show!

1091
00:47:09,451 --> 00:47:12,037
Sorry, I'm sorry. I mean,
we want to do that too, but I apologize.

1092
00:47:12,120 --> 00:47:14,581
It's enough already! Seriously.

1093
00:47:14,665 --> 00:47:16,250
- I'm counting on you.
- Yeah, we should talk.

1094
00:47:16,333 --> 00:47:18,210
- Let's go, Mimi.
- Yeah.

1095
00:47:18,293 --> 00:47:19,127
Let's talk.

1096
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,589
To be honest, man,

1097
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:24,591
when I met you at the beginning, you know…

1098
00:47:25,092 --> 00:47:27,678
I genuinely thought you were a good guy.

1099
00:47:30,389 --> 00:47:32,266
And that's why, like…

1100
00:47:32,349 --> 00:47:36,061
Look, it's fine to come at me
all aggressive, but there are limits.

1101
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:39,356
I apologize for that. I think I also…

1102
00:47:40,023 --> 00:47:41,900
Obviously, I hadn't considered
your feelings

1103
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:44,862
because I was only thinking
about Sara at that time.

1104
00:47:44,945 --> 00:47:47,489
But, truly, I think
this goes for both of us,

1105
00:47:47,573 --> 00:47:50,075
but you're not gonna let any friendship
get in the way of love, right?

1106
00:47:50,158 --> 00:47:53,036
Well, that's true. So, you know,
amongst this group of good guys,

1107
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:55,998
we can get along
except for when it comes to love,

1108
00:47:56,081 --> 00:47:58,000
but there'll definitely
be times when we clash,

1109
00:47:58,083 --> 00:48:00,711
and we talked about facing that
when it happens, right?

1110
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:02,087
We agreed on that.

1111
00:48:03,505 --> 00:48:05,757
So, I don't know what made this so…

1112
00:48:07,843 --> 00:48:10,387
A big part of it is also the fact
that I almost drowned…

1113
00:48:10,470 --> 00:48:12,723
- For that, I'm really sorry.
- It's totally fine.

1114
00:48:12,806 --> 00:48:15,893
I think that was what
sort of made me reach my boiling point.

1115
00:48:15,976 --> 00:48:18,145
Because I was really holding back.

1116
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:20,898
But, regarding that,
you don't have to hold back anymore.

1117
00:48:20,981 --> 00:48:22,941
- If we clash, we clash.
- Yeah, that's true.

1118
00:48:23,025 --> 00:48:24,109
I think that's okay.

1119
00:48:24,192 --> 00:48:25,611
I feel really bad about it.

1120
00:48:25,694 --> 00:48:27,738
I feel like I acted a little immaturely.

1121
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:30,240
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry too.

1122
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:32,534
- Well, but from now on…
- I've calmed down.

1123
00:48:32,618 --> 00:48:35,162
If there happens to be
another time when we clash like this,

1124
00:48:35,245 --> 00:48:37,456
- I intend to face you head-on.
- That's fine by me.

1125
00:48:37,539 --> 00:48:39,708
And I want you
to come face me head-on too.

1126
00:48:40,709 --> 00:48:42,252
Did you guys work it out?

1127
00:48:43,170 --> 00:48:44,588
The clash between men?

1128
00:48:45,631 --> 00:48:46,548
Yeah.

1129
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:49,301
I feel like I acted a bit immaturely.

1130
00:48:49,384 --> 00:48:50,469
Not entirely.

1131
00:48:50,552 --> 00:48:51,678
I don't think you've been--

1132
00:48:51,762 --> 00:48:55,015
I just mean, from now on, I don't want you
to hesitate to clash with me.

1133
00:48:56,975 --> 00:48:57,935
Nice ocean, huh?

1134
00:48:58,518 --> 00:48:59,353
Yeah.

1135
00:49:00,228 --> 00:49:01,605
Well, I feel really bad.

1136
00:49:04,024 --> 00:49:05,901
Let's fix the mood, starting now.

1137
00:49:05,984 --> 00:49:08,236
- As long as we face each other head-on.
- Agreed.

1138
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,530
- Let's not hide what we're thinking.
- Agreed.

1139
00:49:14,159 --> 00:49:15,494
How was the barbecue?

1140
00:49:15,577 --> 00:49:19,456
It was fun, getting to experience
Okinawa for the first time together.

1141
00:49:19,539 --> 00:49:22,334
I was so emotionally unstable today.

1142
00:49:22,417 --> 00:49:24,336
- Yeah, I see.
- I can't help it.

1143
00:49:24,962 --> 00:49:27,297
I'm starting to feel like
I don't know what to do anymore.

1144
00:49:27,381 --> 00:49:29,299
I told him I liked him,
and now he's acting cocky.

1145
00:49:29,383 --> 00:49:31,677
"Well then,
I'll go talk to somebody else."

1146
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:32,719
And off he went.

1147
00:49:33,261 --> 00:49:34,721
He never acted like that before.

1148
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:36,974
It's like, because he knows I like him,

1149
00:49:37,057 --> 00:49:39,184
he's going to someone else
to make me jealous.

1150
00:49:39,267 --> 00:49:41,269
That kind of behavior pissed me off.

1151
00:49:41,353 --> 00:49:43,563
You don't know it was on purpose, though.

1152
00:49:46,024 --> 00:49:48,527
Maybe he just genuinely
wanted to chat with everyone.

1153
00:49:48,610 --> 00:49:50,946
So it's all about how you interpret it.

1154
00:49:51,822 --> 00:49:54,533
How long are you going to keep staying
in that immature mindset?

1155
00:49:55,617 --> 00:49:58,954
I can't help but think
that maybe you're just insecure.

1156
00:49:59,955 --> 00:50:02,708
I mean the point of being here
isn't really to be mature.

1157
00:50:02,791 --> 00:50:03,792
I agree.

1158
00:50:03,875 --> 00:50:06,962
We're here to find love.
And hopefully we can, you know,

1159
00:50:07,045 --> 00:50:08,755
face each other while doing it.

1160
00:50:08,839 --> 00:50:11,174
But you're not making sense.
Like, you're not being consistent.

1161
00:50:11,258 --> 00:50:12,342
Why are you so condescending?

1162
00:50:12,426 --> 00:50:14,970
- Because you're not being consistent.
- Even if I'm not,

1163
00:50:15,053 --> 00:50:18,306
what makes you think you can say things
that are so condescending?

1164
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:21,560
- I'm saying, you won't be liked.
- You say things like that all you want.

1165
00:50:21,643 --> 00:50:24,271
I'm not here to be educated by you.

1166
00:50:24,354 --> 00:50:25,439
And you're free not to listen.

1167
00:50:25,522 --> 00:50:27,274
I'm said I'm not here to be educated,

1168
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:30,068
- yet you're still being condescending.
- I'm just saying, you won't be liked.

1169
00:50:30,152 --> 00:50:31,862
Well, it's not like I'm here to be liked.

1170
00:50:31,945 --> 00:50:33,947
Maybe you should make more of an effort.

1171
00:50:39,870 --> 00:50:41,705
It is happening all over again!

1172
00:50:42,956 --> 00:50:44,750
Am I in my own personal hell?

1173
00:50:45,500 --> 00:50:47,210
- Since last year.
- My apologies.

1174
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:50,422
I come because they told me
that this is a reality dating show.

1175
00:50:51,089 --> 00:50:53,216
And I keep getting shown
footage like this.

1176
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:54,217
I'm sorry, truly.

1177
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:56,178
I'm about to lose my damn mind!
